sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Chef as Chef / Barista
  participant UI as KDS client
  participant BFF as BFF<br/>guards + station access
  participant Kitchen as Kitchen<br/>ticket service
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>KDS projection
  participant Order as Order<br/>item lifecycle
  participant WS as Realtime<br/>hint

  Chef->>UI: Start ticket
  UI->>BFF: POST /tickets/{id}/start<br/>requestId
  BFF->>Kitchen: TCP START_TICKET
  Kitchen->>Redis: Claim command dedupe key
  alt Fresh request
    Kitchen->>Redis: PENDING -> PROCESSING<br/>increment revision
    Kitchen->>WS: Publish TICKET_STARTED
  else Duplicate requestId
    Kitchen-->>BFF: Return current ticket<br/>no second event
  end

  Chef->>UI: Mark ticket done
  UI->>BFF: POST /tickets/{id}/done<br/>requestId
  BFF->>Kitchen: TCP MARK_READY
  Kitchen->>Redis: PROCESSING -> READY<br/>move active to ready queue
  Kitchen->>WS: Publish TICKET_READY
  BFF->>Order: TCP MARK_ITEMS_READY<br/>order item ids
  alt Order sync succeeds
    Order-->>BFF: kitchen.item_ready<br/>order status change if any
    BFF->>WS: Emit staff/customer updates
  else Order sync fails
    BFF->>Kitchen: TCP RECALL_TICKET<br/>compensation requestId
    Kitchen->>Redis: READY -> PROCESSING<br/>within recall window
    Kitchen->>WS: Publish TICKET_RECALLED
  end

  Note over BFF,Order: Kitchen owns KDS ticket state.<br/>Order remains the owner of order item readiness.
